# Factory control panel (Swamp)

When working in this repo, prefer these **approved Swamp operations** over inventing ad-hoc shell for factory ops:

| Intent | Command |
|--------|---------|
| List Ready tickets | `swamp model method run list-ready-tickets execute` |
| Show agent contract | `swamp model method run show-agents-contract execute` |
| Check one ticket | `swamp model method run check-ticket-ready execute` (env `ISSUE_NUMBER`) |
| Run quality gate | `swamp model method run factory-gate execute` (env `SERVICES`) |
| Optional smoke gate | `swamp model method run smoke-gate execute` |
| Run one factory job | `swamp workflow run run-ticket --input issue_number=N --input services=…` |

Also read `AGENTS.md` for hard rules and ticket scope. Tickets live on [Project 10](https://github.com/users/ianckc/projects/10) (`Status = Ready`).

Do **not** invent scope outside the active ticket. Do **not** bypass the gate: leave `just gate` / `factory-gate` green.

Coding still happens here in Cursor; Swamp owns the line (check → pause → gate → bookkeeping).
